    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using `mini.ai`, attempting to use vim `v` to select a single-character target does not work as expected.\n\nHere is an example text:\n```\n(a)\n```\nDo:\n- Put the cursor on letter `a`\n- Click `vib` or `vi(`\n\nThen the `mini.ai` will report:\n```\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"ib\" found covering region within 50 lines and search_method = 'cover_or_next'.\n```\nrather than entering visual mode and select the letter `a`\n\nAnd everything works fine with other verbs like `cib`, `dib`, `yib` in `mini.ai`, only `vib` fails.\nAlso everything works fine with vim default `vib` command, put the cursor on letter `a` then type `:normal! vib`, vim will enter visual mode and select letter `a`.\n\n\nBecause the default `search_method` is `cover_or_next`, Here is another example:\n```\n(a) (b)\n```\nDo:\n- Put the cursor on letter `a`\n- Click `vib` or `vi(`\n\nThen `mini.ai` will move cursor to letter `b` and select it in visual mode.\nBut if you run `cib` `dib` or `yib`, it will do `change` `delete` or `yank` for letter `a`, only `vib` will select letter `b`.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nThis bug can be reproduced with default `min.ai` config\n```lua\nreturn {\n    \"echasnovski/mini.ai\",\n}\n```\nCheck the examples above to reproduce.",
