        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis describes an expected behavior of [consecutive application](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b1dfd15fbf028b76e2d996618d36ae3850f199a2/doc/mini-ai.txt#L128-L130) of textobject in Visual mode (also known as \"incremental selection\" when it is about covering textobjects).\n\nWhat is happening here is that `v` both initiates Visual mode *and* so happens to already select the entire textobject (because it is a single cell). Since the expected textobject is already selected, typing `ib` makes 'mini.ai' think that user want to apply textobject consecutively and thus tries to select another textobject based on the search method:\n- In case of a single `(a)`, there is no such textobject.\n- In case of `(a) (b)` and default `cover_or_next` search method, it selects `b` as it is the next textobject and there is no covering one.\n\nAll in all, this is a side effect of a very useful feature which is impossible to solve (because there is no reasonable way to distinguish whether the user only started Visual mode or already selected an entire textobject). So closing as working as intended.",
